Count a shrunk memory map's merged last entry once.

OcShrinkMemoryMap joins adjacent descriptors into the one before them
(PrevDesc), counting a descriptor into *MemoryMapSize only when it cannot
be joined. PrevDesc is always counted already, so when the map's last
descriptors were merged into it, the closing `+= DescriptorSize` counted
one descriptor too many: the caller got the first entry that had been
merged into PrevDesc a second time, its range inside PrevDesc's. It runs
only under RebuildAppleMemoryMap, which the Snow Leopard config turns on,
and a 4 GiB q35 guest's sorted map ends in RAM above 4 GiB with firmware
allocations beside free memory: the shape that merges at the end. The
kernel is then handed overlapping descriptors.

Applied by internal/firmware's OpenCore build with `git apply`, against
the tree unpacked from the pinned OpenCorePkg tarball. Present in
acidanthera/OpenCorePkg master on 2026-11-03; the same fix is
nfzerox/VirtualIntelMacOnAppleSilicon's
Source/vendor/patches/opencore-memory-map-tail-count.patch (MIT).
docs/decisions/0043.

--- a/Library/OcMemoryLib/MemoryMap.c
+++ b/Library/OcMemoryLib/MemoryMap.c
@@ -425,11 +425,11 @@
   }
 
   //
-  // Handle last entries if they were merged.
+  // packer-plugin-macosx: assets/firmware/patches/0008
+  // When the last entries were merged, they were merged into PrevDesc,
+  // which *MemoryMapSize already counts: counting one more handed the
+  // caller the first merged entry again, overlapping PrevDesc.
   //
-  if (HasEntriesToRemove) {
-    *MemoryMapSize += DescriptorSize;
-  }
 
   return EFI_SUCCESS;
 }
